    "q-342458": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342458",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=-\\sqrt{7}\\,\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-3{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3{x}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
