    "q-342471": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342471",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{5},$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $5{x}^{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{5})}^{2}}\\cdot {({x}^{5})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{10}}\\cdot 5{x}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{1-{x}^{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
