    "q-342666": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342666",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate ${g}^{′}(x)$ for $g(x)={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3).$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)\\,+$ | $4{e}^{x}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the product rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(u\\cdot v)}{\\text{d}x}={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, chain rule, and  formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{x})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3))}^{′} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(4x+3)}^{′} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+\\frac{4{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
